  "case_id": "wave-map-energy",
  "full_target": "Let n,m be positive integers; u:R^n×(0,∞)→R^m jointly smooth and q∈R^m have Euclidean norm one. Assume |u(x,r)|=1; for each (x,r) there is a∈R such that u_tt−Δ_xu=a u; and on each compact interval J⊂(0,∞), u(x,r)=q outside a compact C_J uniformly for r∈J. Define e(x,r)=|u_t|²+Σ_{j=1}^n|∂_{x_j}u|² and E(r)=∫_{R^n}e(x,r)dx, Lebesgue measure, Euclidean norms. Prove e(·,r) is Lebesgue integrable for each r>0, E is differentiable for each r>0, and E'(r)=0.",
  "conclusion": "For every r>0, e(·,r) is Lebesgue integrable, E is differentiable at r, and E'(r)=0.",
